  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">All work is on branch spike/specialist-agents-phase0; nothing in this task is committed to master or to work/specialist-legal-agents-r1 except the results note; a PR, if opened, is titled "[DO NOT MERGE]".</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Both tools sit on the existing /mcp/legal-operations route behind RequireMcpConnectorToken, the rate limit and the kill switch; no new route, server or OAuth registration is added.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-008">Authorization for both tools comes from the existing endpoint-filter chain; the tools add no bypass.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-039">Both tools are read-only (readOnlyHint true) and cataloged; neither writes data or triggers side effects.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-043">spike_review_nda passes profile positions only as inputs declared in the Action input schema (agreement-review or agreement-review-spike per task 010).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Caller resolution uses ICallerSystemUserResolver; an unresolved caller returns isError CALLER_UNRESOLVED and a caller with no test profile returns isError NO_PROFILE; neither path returns another user's profile or a default profile.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Header logging records header names only; values, Authorization, cookies and tokens are never logged or committed (NFR-05).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Spike tests live on the spike branch only; no test is added to master suites.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The spike adds no package reference; publish size stays at master's (.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md).</constraint>
  </constraints>

