  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">git fetch; create spike/specialist-agents-phase0 from origin/master in a separate worktree (never switch branches in the main worktree)</step>
    <step order="2">Fill the real systemuserids for the owner and the test user into copies of the four test profiles placed under the spike branch (read them from DEV read-only)</step>
    <step order="3">Add SpikeGetProfileTool: resolve caller, load test profile by systemuserid, return a data-guarded instruction block plus profileVersion; fail closed</step>
    <step order="4">Add SpikeReviewNdaTool: resolve caller and profile, run the Action via IActionRunner BoundInputs with the positions as declared inputs and the profile tier set explicitly; return the structured review plus profileVersion and latency</step>
    <step order="5">Add header-name logging (names only) on the spike tools</step>
    <step order="6">Write branch tests: NO_PROFILE, CALLER_UNRESOLVED, user A never receives user B's profile, header values never logged</step>
    <step order="7">dotnet build and dotnet test on the branch; push the branch; record the branch SHA in phase0/g3/README.md on work/specialist-legal-agents-r1</step>
    <step order="8">Update tasks/TASK-INDEX.md: change this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` (the bracketed token is mandatory) and set the POML &lt;status&gt; to completed; run pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1</step>
    <step order="9">Record any deviation from the plan in projects/specialist-legal-agents-r1/notes/decisions.md (one dated line)</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If ICallerSystemUserResolver or IActionRunner signatures differ from spec FR-02, STOP and escalate per root CLAUDE.md §6.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the spike would need a new package, route, OAuth registration or a master change, STOP and escalate.</trigger>
    <trigger>If any input, sample or source this task would use contains or references answer-key/ or a real NDA, STOP: do not copy it, and escalate per root CLAUDE.md §6.</trigger>
  </escalation>
  <justification>
    <existing>notes/reuse-scan.md rows "Caller to per-user profile" and "Server-side review with a profile"; CAPABILITY-INDEX row 16 (Action spine); ShowDecisionsTool.cs is the shape to copy</existing>
    <extension>Yes, they wrap existing ICallerSystemUserResolver and IActionRunner; the only new parts are a static test-profile lookup (profile tables are Phase 1) and two branch-only tool classes</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without them G1 variants (a)/(b)/(c) and G3 cannot run, so the D-A7 go/no-go has no evidence</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>
