  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a caller with a test profile, spike_get_profile returns that caller's profile block and its profileVersion.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a caller with no test profile gets isError NO_PROFILE; an unresolved caller gets isError CALLER_UNRESOLVED; neither receives any profile.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a test proves user A never receives user B's profile (both tools).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">spike_review_nda runs agreement-review (or agreement-review-spike) through IActionRunner with the positions as declared inputs and the profile tier applied, returning the review, profileVersion and latency.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a test proves header values, Authorization and cookies are never logged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">dotnet build and dotnet test pass on the spike branch; master has no new commit from this task.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named above; anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Use a throwaway worktree for the spike branch (never switch the project worktree). Seeding proof requested for the profile-isolation guard only (tenant-isolation outcome).</notes>

